        {
          "text": "Larkhollow Community Hospital's Medical Staff Office credentials every practitioner who applies for membership and clinical privileges: it collects the application, verifies each element with the source that owns it, chases what has not come back, presents a complete file to the committees, and records what the Governing Body decides. One person does this work, by hand, for every file at once, and the office needs it run the same way every time — so that nothing is presented incomplete, nothing stale carries forward, and no privilege is ever active before the approval that grants it. The hospital, its practitioners and its records are fictional.",
