      "content": "Application for initial appointment and clinical privileges — blank form\nLarkhollow Community Hospital · Medical Staff Office Form version LARK-APP-2026.1. This is the blank form. A completed form becomes revision 1 of an application; a correction becomes revision 2, and so on. A revision never replaces the one before it in the file.\nComplete every section. An incomplete application is returned with a written list of what is missing, and the reply is due within 30 calendar days of the date on that letter.\nSection A — Identity and contact\nField\nWhat to enter\nLast name, First name, Middle name\nAs shown on your licence. Leave middle name blank only if you have none\nBirth year\nFour digits\nDegree\nMD or DO\nNational Provider Identifier\nTen digits, if you hold one. This is an identifier for billing and is not a licence. Entering it does not declare a licence\nPractice state\nThe two-letter state in which you will see patients under this appointment\nPosition sought\nThe role this appointment is for\nClinical discipline\nThe discipline you practise, chosen from: Family Medicine, Internal Medicine, Hospital Medicine, Cardiovascular Disease, Emergency Medicine, General Surgery, Obstetrics and Gynecology, Pediatrics, Anesthesiology, Diagnostic Radiology, Psychiatry, Orthopaedic Surgery. Your peer referees must practise the discipline you name here\nSection B — Authorization and release\nI authorize Larkhollow Community Hospital to request and receive information about me from any school, training programme, licensing board, certifying board, employer, affiliated institution and professional reference named in this application, and I authorize each of them to release it. I release each of them from liability for doing so.\nSignature and date. Until this is signed and dated, the office sends no verification request of any kind, and the application cannot advance.\nSection C — Privileges requested\nList every privilege group you request, by the code and name published in the current privilege criteria. Name the criteria version you are requesting under. At least one group is required.\nSection D — Education and post-graduate training\nOne row per entry. Medical school first, then every internship, residency, fellowship or other organized professional training, in date order.\nField\nWhat to enter\nEntry type\nmedical-school, residency, fellowship, or other\nOrganization, Location\nThe school or sponsoring institution, and its town and state\nRole\nDegree sought, or the programme and position\nFrom date, To date\nYYYY-MM-DD, inclusive\nVerification contact name and email\nWhom the office should write to\nSection E — Employment, affiliations, teaching and military service\nOne row per entry, in date order, running continuously from the day after you finished professional school to today.\nField\nWhat to enter\nEntry type\nemployment, affiliation, teaching, military, or other\nOrganization, Location\nThe employer or institution, and its town and state\nRole\nYour position\nFrom date, To date\nYYYY-MM-DD, inclusive. Leave To date blank only if the entry is current\nHours per week\nWhole hours. A part-time entry is still an entry\nVerification contact name and email\nWhom the office should write to\nNotes\nAnything the dates alone do not explain\nOverlapping entries are expected — a part-time clinic post alongside a hospital appointment is two entries, not an error. Enter both.\nSection F — Explanation of periods not covered\nFor every period of 30 days or more since you finished professional school that no entry in Section D or E covers, attach a written explanation. One explanation per period. Begin the explanation with the line Period explained: <from date> to <to date>, and make sure that period covers the whole of the period you are explaining — the office matches your explanation to the period by those two dates and by nothing else.\nThe office records your explanation. The office does not judge it. Whether an explanation is satisfactory is the Clinical Director's decision.\nAn application with a period of 30 days or more and no written explanation for it is returned as incomplete.\nSection G — Licences and certifications\nOne row per credential, including every licence and certification you have ever held, active or inactive, in any state and from any board.\nField\nWhat to enter\nClass\nlicence or certification\nIssuer\nThe state board or the certifying board\nJurisdiction or board\nTwo-letter state for a licence; the board's short code for a certification\nNumber\nThe credential number\nStatus\nYour own description: Active, Inactive, Expired, Board certified, Board eligible\nIssue date, Expiry date\nYYYY-MM-DD\nWhat you enter here is your declaration. The office verifies each entry with the issuing board, and the board's answer is what goes in the file.\nSection H — Peer references\nName at least two peer referees. For each: name, credential, organization, specialty, working address, and how you have worked together.\nA referee must have worked directly with you within the past two years, must practise in the same clinical discipline, and must not be a relative, spouse or partner. The office writes to each referee directly; a reference you carry to us yourself cannot be used.\nSection I — Professional practice questions\nAnswer every question Yes or No. Every Yes requires a written explanation in the comment box beside it. Leaving a question unanswered makes the application incomplete.\nCode\nQuestion\nPPQ-1\nHas any licence or registration you hold or have held ever been denied, suspended, revoked, restricted, placed on probation, made subject to a monitoring agreement, surrendered, or subjected to any other action by a licensing board?\nPPQ-2\nHave your clinical privileges at any institution ever been denied, reduced, restricted, suspended, revoked, not renewed, or made subject to conditions?\nPPQ-3\nHave you ever resigned from, or withdrawn an application to, a medical staff or training programme while an investigation was pending or in exchange for not conducting an investigation?\nPPQ-4\nHas any board certification you hold or have held ever been revoked, suspended, or not renewed for cause?\nPPQ-5\nHave you ever been the subject of a professional review action reportable to a national data bank?\nPPQ-6\nHave you ever been excluded, debarred or suspended from participation in a federal or state health care programme?\nPPQ-7\nHave you ever been convicted of, or pleaded guilty or no contest to, a criminal offence other than a minor traffic violation?\nPPQ-8\nIs there any physical or mental condition, or any use of a substance, that currently impairs your ability to perform the privileges you are requesting, with or without accommodation?\nA Yes to any of these is a high-risk finding. It is not by itself a bar to appointment. It is routed to the Clinical Director and presented to the Executive Committee of the Medical Staff and to the Governing Body with the evidence.\nIf a verification the office receives shows that a Yes was owed and a No was given, the office will contact you to confirm the answer before the file goes any further.\nSection J — Attestation\nI attest that everything in this application is complete, current and correct. I understand that the burden of supplying verifiable information is mine, and that a discrepancy between what I have declared and what a source reports will be put back to me in writing.\nSignature and date.\nWhat the office does with a completed form\nThe office records receipt, screens the nine completeness conditions in the procedure, and either takes the file up or writes to you with the missing items. It then writes to the schools, programmes, boards, employers, affiliations and referees named above. It does not use anything you hand over yourself in place of their replies."
