      "content": "Professional peer reference — blank request and return form\nLarkhollow Community Hospital · Medical Staff Office Form version LARK-REF-2026.1.\nThe office sends this form directly to the referee the applicant named, and the referee returns it directly to the office. A form that reaches us through the applicant cannot be used.\nPart 1 — completed by the Medical Staff Office before sending\nField\nContent\nReferee identifier\nThe office's identifier for this referee on this file\nApplicant\nName and degree\nPrivileges requested\nThe privilege groups on the application\nRequest date\nThe date this request was sent\nRequest number\n1, 2 or 3 — each reminder is a fresh numbered request\nWe write up to three times, 21 calendar days apart. If no reply has reached us by the 64th day after the first request, we tell the applicant and ask for an additional referee. The original request stays open. We do not close it as satisfied and we do not count it.\nPart 2 — completed by the referee\nField\nWhat to enter\nAre you a relative, spouse or partner of the applicant?\nTick Yes or No. This box is never left blank\nRelationship\nHow you worked with the applicant, in your own words\nYour specialty\nThe clinical discipline you practise, chosen from the same list the applicant chose from: Family Medicine, Internal Medicine, Hospital Medicine, Cardiovascular Disease, Emergency Medicine, General Surgery, Obstetrics and Gynecology, Pediatrics, Anesthesiology, Diagnostic Radiology, Psychiatry, Orthopaedic Surgery — or your own discipline if it is not on that list\nDates you worked directly together\nFirst and last date. Leave the last date blank only if you still work together\nRecommendation\nRecommend without reservation, Recommend, Recommend with reservations, or Do not recommend\nComments\nCharacter, clinical experience, competency, and anything else you want on the record\nSignature and signature date\nThe date you sign. This is the date we measure currency from — not the date we receive the form\nWho may give a peer reference\nThree conditions, each independent, all three required:\nyou have worked directly with the applicant within the two years ending on the day you sign this form;\nyou practise in the same clinical discipline as the applicant;\nyou are not a relative, spouse or partner of the applicant.\nIf any one of the three does not hold, say so on the form and return it anyway. We will record your reply, and we will not count it towards the two references the appointment needs. That is not a judgment about you or about the applicant; it is the rule we apply to every file the same way.\nCurrency\nA reference is current if the signature date is within two years of the date the file is presented to the Governing Body. A reference signed a long time before the file is presented stops being current, and we ask again.\nPart 3 — completed by the Medical Staff Office on return\nField\nContent\nReceived date\nThe date the completed form reached the office\nHow it arrived\nSecure portal, letter, fax or email, direct from the referee\nNothing in Part 2 is edited, summarized or corrected by the office. What the referee wrote is what goes in the file, including a relationship or a specialty that differs from what the applicant told us."
