      "content": "# Batch 3 export — Larkhollow Community Hospital, Medical Staff Office\n\n**Export date: 2026-05-18**\n**Window covered: 2026-04-20 to 2026-05-17**\n\nThis folder is a closed export. Nothing in it happened after 2026-05-18, and nothing in it will be\nedited. Work it as if today were the export date.\n\nThis export carries what changed between 2026-04-20 and 2026-05-17. The state board lookup is again a re-run against the practitioners with an open file.\n\n## What is here\n\n| File | Rows |\n|---|---|\n| `applications.csv` | 1 |\n| `application-disclosures.csv` | 8 |\n| `declared-history.csv` | 5 |\n| `declared-credentials.csv` | 3 |\n| `privilege-requests.csv` | 1 |\n| `licence-lookup-wa.csv` | 40 |\n| `licence-lookup-other-states.csv` | 0 |\n| `certification-replies.csv` | 0 |\n| `verification-replies.csv` | 3 |\n| `verification-attempts.csv` | 5 |\n| `peer-referees.csv` | 4 |\n| `peer-reference-replies.csv` | 4 |\n| `correspondence.csv` | 26 |\n\n| Folder | Documents |\n|---|---|\n| `letters/` | 4 |\n| `dispositions/` | 1 |\n| `decisions/` | 21 |\n\nA file with only a header row means the export ran and this window produced nothing of that kind.\nThat is not a missing file.\n\nThe field dictionary, the join rules, the meaning of every blank and the rarity of an adverse\nboard finding are in `../../office/export-notes.md`. The office's procedure is in\n`../../office/procedure-extract.md`. Read both before working this folder.\n\n— Renata Kowalczyk, CPMSM, Medical Services Professional\n"
